sequenceDiagram
    actor U as User
    participant B as Browser
    participant MW as Edge Middleware
    participant NA as /api/auth/[...nextauth]
    participant Auth as lib/auth (NextAuth options)
    participant Adapter as lib/auth/prisma-adapter
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    %% --- Initial gated visit ---------------------------------------------
    U->>B: Navigate to /admin
    B->>MW: GET /admin (no cookie)
    MW->>MW: getToken() — no NextAuth session cookie
    MW-->>B: 302 Redirect /login?callbackUrl=/admin

    %% --- Credentials sign-in ---------------------------------------------
    U->>B: Submit email + password on /login
    B->>NA: POST /api/auth/callback/credentials
    NA->>Auth: authorize({ email, password })
    Auth->>DB: findUnique({ email })
    DB-->>Auth: User row
    Auth->>Auth: verifyPassword(input, passwordHash) via bcryptjs
    Auth->>Adapter: create/update Session row
    Auth-->>NA: User payload { id, email, role }
    NA->>Auth: signIn callback (link Azure AD if applicable)
    NA->>Auth: jwt callback — inject { userId, role }
    NA->>Auth: session callback — hydrate session
    NA-->>B: 200 + Set-Cookie next-auth.session-token (HttpOnly, encrypted JWT, 30d)

    %% --- Subsequent gated request ----------------------------------------
    B->>MW: GET /admin (with session cookie)
    MW->>MW: getToken() — decrypt session JWT
    MW->>MW: Check role in admin or superadmin
    MW->>MW: Set headers x-request-id, x-nonce,\n  x-user-id, x-user-email, x-user-role
    MW-->>B: 200 Admin page + per-request CSP header

    %% --- Azure AD SSO branch ---------------------------------------------
    Note over B,NA: SSO branch (Microsoft Entra ID)
    U->>B: Click "Sign in with Microsoft"
    B->>NA: GET /api/auth/signin/azure-ad
    NA-->>B: 302 to Microsoft authorize endpoint
    B->>NA: GET /api/auth/callback/azure-ad?code=...
    NA->>Auth: signIn callback — link Account to existing User\n  (or create User if first sign-in)
    NA->>Adapter: upsert Account row { provider: azure-ad }
    NA-->>B: Set-Cookie session-token + redirect to callbackUrl

    %% --- Token revocation / sign-out ------------------------------------
    Note over Auth: lib/auth/token-revocation supports
    Note over Auth: per-device sign-out via JWT id blacklist
